L76: Hierarchical clustering showed that all samples from the same supplementation group (according to the supplement type, time point and sex) grouped well based on the similarity of the gene expression profiles (  Figure 1  ). GSEA was conducted on a list of differentially expressed genes (  p  <0.05) with a fold change of >1.0 (obtained from Partek analysis) to identify the functional categories of the genes. Fisher’s exact test was performed to compute the  p  values in order to determine the overlap between the entities (gene set) and pathways. The gene ontology (pathway) was ranked based on the highest  p  value (Supplementary Table S1-S8).
